id=abk_runtime_tunables
name=ABK 5.15 Runtime Tunables
version=v0.6.2
versionCode=8
author=FanZiyun
description=Drives the ABK 5.15 kernel grafts that are otherwise inert on device: keeps the zram algorithm policy in force at every boot (primary lz4kd, secondary zstd, locked in the kernel by Batch 11 and re-asserted here on older kernels), preserves or establishes the zram writeback backing device instead of trading it away, runs age-based recompression sweeps through the async worker, follows each sweep with one gated zsmalloc compaction pass, records who owns CPU frequency at boot (a vendor FAS/WALT governor must keep it, since Batch 10-5 ships the smart-freq floor off), and reports or tunes the remaining runtime knobs (MGLRU, THP, swappiness, abk_sf, dynamic readahead, cgroup-v1 proactive reclaim).
